pyTBkit is a native Python implementation informed by TBkit by BUAA-TCMP
and its contributors: https://github.com/BUAA-TCMP/TBkit .
The reviewed canonical MATLAB commit is pinned in upstream.json.
Development originally started from X-T-Zeng/TBkit commit
290224bfb0312e8f6f320fe930ff79ed7a45ed2c; that fork is historical context,
not the current MATLAB reference.
This implementation, examples, tests and proposed upstream patches are
provided under GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1. See LICENSE.
Reference tests execute selected official MATLAB numerical functions via
Octave with explicit data/page-algebra adapters; this does not certify
all MATLAB classes or the commercial MATLAB Symbolic Math Toolbox.
